title: "agent-approval-gate"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/agent-approval-gate"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/agent-approval-gate"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free approval gate for unattended agents. When an agent hits an action it
  must not decide alone, or physically cannot perform, the ask goes to a messenger, the
  answer comes back into the run, silence is re-pinged, escalated and finally abandoned
  rather than resurrected. Its substance is the decision-class table: internal, own-channel
  and short third-party actions are refused by exit code from ever reaching a human, so
  only human-hands and money or irreversible or legal actions can queue. Authority is the
  approver's sender id, never text claiming approval, which makes it resistant to
  instructions found in fetched content. Ships a Telegram reference transport, a
  supervisor, an autonomy counter and 36 stdlib tests.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - human-in-the-loop
  - approval-workflow
  - agent-safety
  - prompt-injection
  - autonomy
